From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000
Subject: Run transform propagation as one schedule that can run more than once a frame
Date: 2026-11-23T20:06:25+00:00

mark_dirty_trees, propagate_parent_transforms and sync_simple_transforms
move into their own schedule, PropagateTransforms, which
TransformPropagate runs through propagate_transforms in PostStartup and
PostUpdate. An app that needs current globals earlier in the frame (the
explorer runs a pass ahead of its collider, player and camera updates) runs
the same schedule there.

Change detection is relative to a system's previous run. With a second
instance of the three systems, each instance's previous run was a frame
ago, so each walked every tree that the other had just walked: the late
pass re-marked and re-propagated everything the early pass had done that
frame, and the early pass did the same with the late pass's work from the
frame before. With one instance run twice, each run sees only the changes
since the other.
